8230	{"artifactId":"LLD-3b6bd6b5fa3c30d1-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-3b6bd6b5fa3c30d1-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:31:20.869Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers every part of the ISSUE's fix intent: one fake DOM (including the inert dgPickRef document at :5315), one flatten, one opener, guards on git and tsc that skip with a reason, every assertion kept, and test-only scope.","evidence":"ISSUE.md fix intent, lines 44-48, lists five bullets. LLD §3.1 deletes stubEl/node/frNode/dgNode/uxNodeStub and the local bodyStub, and builds the loaders 'and the dgPickRef documents' from bodyStub. The inline doc at test.ts:5314-5316 is `{ createElement: () => ({}), createElementNS: () => ({}) }`. §2.2 merges the four flattens, §2.3 the openers, and §2.4/§2.5 guard tsc and git. The invariants keep every assertion and change no production file. [files: docs/standalone/defects-review-pane-s-test-file-E202610093b6bd6b5/ISSUE.md, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today's fakes behave as the design says. bodyStub keeps listeners as arrays and clears children on textContent and innerHTML (parsing TAG\\ttext). StubNode stores one listener per type. uxNodeStub records writes, traps innerHTML/outerHTML, does not clear children on textContent, and has text nodes { nodeType: 3, data }.","evidence":"test.ts:1543 `listeners: Record<string, Array<() => void>>`, :1555-1566 innerHTML setter parses `TAG\\ttext` and `set textContent(v) { txt = v; html = ''; children.length = 0; }`. :722 `addEventListener(k, fn) { this.listeners[k] = fn; }`. :4106-4117: the textContent setter only records the write, and the innerHTML/outerHTML trap loop records each write. :4089 `interface UxTextNode { nodeType: 3; data: string }`. :4161-4164 uxFlatten skips isText children. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"openAndGetContent has 6 callers, and the two openers together have 18 call sites (LLD §2.3, migration step 4, ac3 mapping).","evidence":"A grep of docs-review-panel.test.ts finds openAndGetContent( called at :621, :637 (once, inside a for loop), :645, :666 and :689, which is 5 callers, not 6. openWithContent( is called at :976, :990, :2316, :2353, :2367, :3755, :3796, :3814, :3832, :3856 and :3881, which is 11. The total is 16, not 18. The merge itself is still right, but the counts the ac3 proof relies on are wrong. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts]","action":"Correct the counts to 5 openAndGetContent callers and 16 opener call sites in total, in §2.3, migration step 4 and the ac3 mapping.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every git and tsc site is listed: the direct execFileSync git show calls at :1501 and :3567, the local git helper at :4010 used at :4023-:4030, the direct log/diff calls at :5648-:5655, and the tsc existence asserts at :2449 and :2549.","evidence":"Grepping for `execFileSync('git'` finds exactly :1501, :3567, :4011 (inside the helper at :4010) and :5648/:5652/:5655. typescript/bin/tsc is resolved only at :2448 and :2548, with the asserts at :2449 and :2549. typecheckAgainstPanel (:2447) is called at :2479 and :2492 from a test declared `() =>`, so that test also needs a `t` parameter. That is implied by the signature change. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Clearing children on every textContent assignment keeps all 200 tests passing, because the renderers set textContent before they append children.","evidence":"Every `textContent=` in the shipped renderer sources (docs-review-panel.ts:97, 132, 137, 149, 200-235, 498, 777-791, 898, 1629-1733) assigns text to a freshly created element before anything is appended, e.g. `st.textContent=r.statement;it.appendChild(st)` and uxTextNode at :898. I found no case that sets textContent on an element after giving it children, so the stricter rule should not cause failures. The design still treats any such failure as a finding (§4) instead of weakening the fake. uxAllText (:4168) reads both textContent and text-node children, and that keeps working. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Changing the :807/:826 listener calls to fire every listener in the array keeps those assertions' behaviour.","evidence":":807 and :826 call `sel.listeners['change']!()` against StubNode's one listener per type (:722). The chooser registers one change listener, so firing each entry of the array gives the same `picked` results asserted at :808 and :827. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Each acceptance criterion has a test that would fail without the fix. In particular, ac3 (one opener) is proven by a test.","evidence":"ac4 has a real failing-first test: the recording-context guard tests and 'history and compiler checks skip with a stated reason…' need git(t, need) and typecheckAgainstPanel(t, …), which do not exist yet. ac1 and ac2 have new fake-dom.test.ts contract tests. The ac3 entry is 'the 18 former … call sites pass through the one openWithContent'. That is the existing suite, which passes today with two openers, so nothing would fail if openAndGetContent were left in place. The figure 18 is also wrong; there are 16 call sites (see current-behaviour). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts]","action":"Give ac3 a check that fails without the fix: for example, a source scan asserting that the file declares exactly one opener (no `function openAndGetContent`), plus a direct test that openWithContent(string) and openWithContent({markdown, openQuestions: [], blocked: false}) return identical payloads.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-09T13:31:20.869Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{"current-behaviour.2":{"findingId":"current-behaviour.2","status":"resolved","note":"Applied. grep confirms 6 openAndGetContent( and 12 openWithContent( occurrences, each count including the definition. That is 5 callers plus 11 callers, 16 opener call sites in all. The figures are corrected in openWithContent's postconditions, migration step 4 and the ac3 mapping.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-09T13:32:47.835Z"},"tests.1":{"findingId":"tests.1","status":"resolved","note":"Applied. ac3 now has a failing-first test: 'there is one document opener, and a markdown string and the same markdown as DocsContent open to identical payloads'. It is a source scan asserting the file has no openAndGetContent declaration and exactly one openWithContent, plus a direct equality check of the two payloads. It fails while openAndGetContent still exists.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-09T13:32:47.836Z"}}}}}}
